From d43e6b7b05574f5b8653186105667acb9b1ffba6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 15:56:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0195 -- freeze at chosen ticks for an
 emulated-screen capture; DOSAGS_BREAK_0193 as the gate's control

Instrument only; both knobs are off unless their variable is set, and neither is for a timed cell. Both are in the
manifest env allowlist, and tests/harness/run-hw.sh refuses to start a hardware cell that sets either unless its tag begins
DIAG.

Why. The present verifier (ags 0192) answers "do the pushed rects cover what the engine drew". It cannot answer "did the
screen come out the same as a full push", and the alias-rung screen was found incomplete while it read zero: with the alias
on, the engine's frame IS the window surface, so a region never drawn into it reads equal to a shadow that was never
written. A screen-level comparison needs two runs captured at the SAME tick, which a wall-clock capture cannot give
because content changes every tick.

DOSAGS_FREEZE_TICKS=a,b,c: the first rendered tick at or after each value writes FRZnn.TXT (idx, wanted tick, actual tick)
into the current directory and spins for DOSAGS_FREEZE_MS (default 1200), so the screen is static while a host watcher
photographs it. On DOSBox-X the current directory is a host directory. The fixed-timestep loop then catches up at most
MAX_CATCHUP ticks and resyncs, the same in both runs being compared; a "DOS-PORT freeze" line records the actual tick so
a comparison whose ticks differ is void rather than silently wrong.

DOSAGS_BREAK_0193=1 turns off both parts of ags 0193 (carried marks and the full latch at the two whole-surface
invalidators), reproducing the 0192-era under-push, so the screen-equality gate can be shown to FAIL on a known-bad
build instead of only ever being seen to pass.

Removal condition. A switch that re-breaks a shipped fix should not exist in a shipped binary. Both knobs are to be REMOVED
(not merely defaulted off) by the release-packaging patch series, before any release artefact is cut; PLAN.md's
instrumentation inventory tracks it as open. Until then they are diagnostics: allowlisted so a run that used one hashes
differently, and refused on hardware outside a DIAG-tagged cell.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017rABavUPepUfapaKZYKPvD
